# 7. Four Pillars of OOP

The four major pillars of Object-Oriented Programming are:

```text
             OOP
              |
      +-------+-------+
      |       |       |
 Encapsulation      Abstraction
      |               |
      +-------+-------+
              |
       +------+------+
       |             |
   Inheritance   Polymorphism
```

## Quick Revision

| Pillar               | Main Idea                     | Easy Question                |
| -------------------- | ----------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| 🔒 **Encapsulation** | Hide/protect data             | "How do I protect the data?" |
| 🎭 **Abstraction**   | Hide complexity               | "What should I expose?"      |
| 🧬 **Inheritance**   | Reuse/extend behavior         | "IS-A relationship?"         |
| 🔄 **Polymorphism**  | One interface, many behaviors | "Can it behave differently?" |

